From: SoundTap contributors <soundtap@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Retry the audio key request

The session waits 1.5 s for an audio key. Right after connecting, on a
speaker whose Wi-Fi is still settling, the first answer can come later.
Without the key the player downloads the whole file, the decoder fails
on it and the track is skipped: the first track after boot stayed silent
for about 17 s and was then dropped. Ask up to three times.

Upstream: Not submitted
Signed-off-by: Stein Milder <info@steinmilder.nl>

---
  playback/src/player.rs | 12 +++++++++++-
  1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/playback/src/player.rs b/playback/src/player.rs
index 9c09be5..1f03644 100644
--- a/playback/src/player.rs
+++ b/playback/src/player.rs
@@ -1076,7 +1076,17 @@ impl PlayerTrackLoader {
             // Not all audio files are encrypted. If we can't get a key, try loading the track
             // without decryption. If the file was encrypted after all, the decoder will fail
             // parsing and bail out, so we should be safe from outputting ear-piercing noise.
-            let key = match self.session.audio_key().request(track_id, file_id).await {
+            // The first key request after connecting can take longer than the 1.5 s the
+            // session waits, and a track without its key is downloaded whole, fails to decode
+            // and is skipped. Ask up to three times before giving up.
+            let mut key_result = self.session.audio_key().request(track_id, file_id).await;
+            for _ in 1..3 {
+                if key_result.is_ok() {
+                    break;
+                }
+                key_result = self.session.audio_key().request(track_id, file_id).await;
+            }
+            let key = match key_result {
                 Ok(key) => Some(key),
                 Err(e) => {
                     warn!("Unable to load key, continuing without decryption: {e}");
